<!--
  A plain padlock — the design system's generic "Lock" utility glyph
  (`LockIcon` in `src/ui/components/icons.tsx`), transcribed 1:1 from its
  own 24×24, 1.8px-stroke path data. `viewportWidth/Height` match
  `LockIcon`'s own 24×24 viewBox 1:1, so `pathData` below is copied, not
  rescaled.

  STALE REFERENCE, fixed as of the visual-parity doc pass (see
  docs/ime-visual-parity-plan.md): this used to say "Used for the IME
  keypad's Lock key" — that key moved to the top bar entirely
  (`buildTopBarLockButton`, `docs/ime-ux-redesign-proposal.md`'s own
  "Proposed layout"/"Status: built"), so there is no keypad Lock key any
  more for this to describe; the top bar is this drawable's only current
  call site (`R.drawable.ic_lock` in `VaultKeyboardView.kt`).

  The baked-in stroke color below is a placeholder only, same reasoning as
  `ic_globe.xml`'s own doc: the top bar tints it `setColorFilter(SUCCESS)`
  at render time, not this literal. Kept in sync by hand anyway, for
  consistency rather than correctness — currently `#D6E4EF`
  (`FOREGROUND`'s real value as of the visual-parity pass; was `#E2E6EA`,
  the never-fully-applied vault-fg CSS-token attempt before that, and
  `#B8CEDF` before that: three palettes deep, all superseded). The CSS
  token's own usual leading pair of hyphens is spelled out as a word here,
  never as the two literal characters back to back: an XML comment may not
  contain that pair anywhere in its body, and an earlier revision of this
  exact paragraph broke the real Gradle resource build by doing exactly
  that — a real, compiler-caught bug no brace/paren balance check
  (this project's own usual substitute for one) could ever have caught.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:pathData="M6 10H18A2 2 0 0 1 20 12V18A2 2 0 0 1 18 20H6A2 2 0 0 1 4 18V12A2 2 0 0 1 6 10Z"
        android:strokeColor="#D6E4EF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"/>
    <path
        android:pathData="M8 10V7a4 4 0 1 1 8 0v3"
        android:strokeColor="#D6E4EF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"/>
</vector>
